<h1>JanCare: The Director's Cut Production Script</h1>
<p><strong>Smart India Hackathon (SIH) Grand Finale Master Video Blueprint</strong> | Duration: 04:55 Min | Format: 1080p 60 FPS</p>
<hr/>

<table style="width: 100%; background-color: #f8fafc; border: 1pt solid #e2e8f0;">
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Target Duration:</strong> 04:55 Minutes</td>
    <td><strong>Quality / FPS:</strong> 1080p, 60 FPS</td>
    <td><strong>Speech Pacing:</strong> 130 WPM</td>
    <td><strong>Core Stack:</strong> IndexedDB, WebRTC, Next.js</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>🎬 PROLOGUE: The 70-20 Dilemma & The Broken Lifeline (00:00 - 00:40)</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 15%;">Timestamp</th>
    <th style="width: 40%;">Screen & Visual Choreography</th>
    <th style="width: 45%;">Voiceover & Audio Direction</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>0:00 - 0:15</strong></td>
    <td><strong>[CINEMATIC MONTAGE]</strong> Dark backdrop. Fast data-card reveals: <em>"70% Population Rural vs. 20% Specialists"</em>. Visual zooms into a rural tribal pocket (Igatpuri/Sinnar) and a smartphone showing <strong>"No Service / Emergency Only"</strong>.</td>
    <td><em>(SFX: Low Rhythmic Bass Tension Pulse)</em><br/>
    <div class="quote">"Across rural India, 800 million citizens rely on healthcare that is fundamentally fragmented. When a critical symptom strikes in a remote tribal hamlet, the lifeline is broken before it even begins."</div></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>0:15 - 0:28</strong></td>
    <td><strong>[SPLIT SCREEN]</strong> Left: Rural patient with a paper prescription.<br/>Right: Private pharmacy bill reading <strong>₹65,000 (Catastrophic Medical Debt)</strong>.</td>
    <td><div class="quote">"Zero network connectivity stops vital intake. Misdiagnosis delays life-saving interventions. And commercial branded medicines push families into crushing generational debt."</div></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>0:28 - 0:40</strong></td>
    <td><strong>[LOGO REVEAL]</strong> Screen clears. <strong>JanCare</strong> tricolor emblem ignites with tagline: <em>"India’s Offline-First, AI-Triaged Digital Healthcare Stack"</em>.</td>
    <td><em>(SFX: Uplifting Technology Cymbal Swell)</em><br/>
    <div class="quote">"We built JanCare: India’s first offline-first, WHO-protocol governed digital healthcare ecosystem that unites frontline ASHA workers, specialist doctors, Ayushman Bharat PM-JAY, and Jan Aushadhi Kendras into one unbroken continuum."</div></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>🏛️ ACT I: The Architectural Blueprint & The 5 Pillars (00:40 - 01:20)</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 15%;">Timestamp</th>
    <th style="width: 40%;">Screen & Visual Choreography</th>
    <th style="width: 45%;">Voiceover & Audio Direction</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>0:40 - 01:00</strong></td>
    <td><strong>[INFOGRAPHIC DIAGRAM]</strong> Full display of the 5-Stage Healthcare Journey Infographic. Animated highlight pulses sequentially through: <em>1. Offline ASHA, 2. Multilingual AI, 3. Teleconsult, 4. PM-JAY Cashless, 5. Jan Aushadhi</em>.</td>
    <td><div class="quote">"Unlike conventional tele-health apps that crash without 5G, JanCare is engineered from the ground up to operate in extreme connectivity constraints while adhering 100% to India's Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission (ABDM) standards."</div></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>01:00 - 01:20</strong></td>
    <td><strong>[ROLE DASHBOARD GRID]</strong> Quick transition showcasing the 5 live portal interfaces (ASHA, Patient, Doctor, Pharmacist, District Admin).</td>
    <td><div class="quote">"Let us now step into a real clinical case: Patient Ramesh Patil, a 46-year-old farmer in a zero-connectivity tribal village, experiencing sudden acute chest discomfort."</div></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>📱 ACT II: Frontline ASHA Offline Engine & Zero-Drop Sync (01:20 - 02:05)</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 15%;">Timestamp</th>
    <th style="width: 40%;">Screen Action (/asha/dashboard)</th>
    <th style="width: 45%;">Voiceover & Audio Direction</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>01:20 - 01:35</strong></td>
    <td><strong>[ZOOM ON NETWORK TOGGLE]</strong> 1. Open ASHA Dashboard.<br/>2. Toggle <strong>"Simulate Offline Mode"</strong> switch.<br/>3. Top banner turns: <strong>"🔴 Offline Mode (IndexedDB Active)"</strong>.</td>
    <td><div class="quote">"ASHA worker Sunita visits Ramesh's home in a tribal hamlet with zero cellular network. She activates JanCare's Offline Mode. The entire application runs client-side with zero dependency on active servers."</div></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>01:35 - 01:50</strong></td>
    <td><strong>[VITAL INTAKE]</strong> 1. Sunita registers Ramesh Patil (Age 46, Nashik/Sinnar).<br/>2. Records vitals: <strong>BP 148/92 mmHg, SpO2 94%, Severe Chest Discomfort</strong>.<br/>3. Clicks <strong>"Save to Local Offline Cache"</strong>.<br/>4. Offline Queue: <strong>[ 1 Pending Record ]</strong>.</td>
    <td><div class="quote">"She records Ramesh's blood pressure, oxygen saturation, and clinical symptoms. JanCare encrypts and stores the telemetry inside browser IndexedDB, instantly queuing it for background synchronization."</div></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>01:50 - 02:05</strong></td>
    <td><strong>[1-CLICK CLOUD SYNC]</strong> 1. Network toggle returns to <strong>"🟢 Online"</strong>.<br/>2. Click <strong>"Sync to Central Cloud"</strong>.<br/>3. Green toast: <em>"Patient Ramesh Patil synced with District Health Registry"</em>.</td>
    <td><em>(SFX: Clean Success Ping)</em><br/>
    <div class="quote">"The moment connectivity is detected, JanCare’s synchronization engine flushes the queue to the central health registry without duplicate records or packet drops."</div></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>🎙️ ACT III: Multilingual AI Voice Triage & WHO Guidelines (02:05 - 02:50)</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 15%;">Timestamp</th>
    <th style="width: 40%;">Screen Action (/patient/dashboard)</th>
    <th style="width: 45%;">Voiceover & Audio Direction</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>02:05 - 02:25</strong></td>
    <td><strong>[VERNACULAR VOICE]</strong> 1. Switch portal language to <strong>मराठी (Marathi)</strong>.<br/>2. Click floating microphone.<br/>3. Play Marathi audio: <em>"माझ्या छातीत खूप दुखत आहे आणि डाव्या हाताला मुंग्या येत आहेत"</em>.<br/>4. Live audio waveform transcribes Marathi text in real time.</td>
    <td><div class="quote">"For rural citizens who cannot type, JanCare provides voice-first intake in native vernacular languages including Marathi, Hindi, and Odia. Ramesh simply speaks his symptoms into his phone."</div></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>02:25 - 02:50</strong></td>
    <td><strong>[ZOOM ON CLINICAL RULE TAG]</strong> Triage Card appears:<br/>• Priority: <strong>High Priority / Emergency</strong><br/>• Specialist: <strong>Cardiology (Dr. Smita Rao)</strong><br/>• Protocol: <strong>WHO/IMHA Standard Protocol #C-104</strong></td>
    <td><div class="quote">"Crucially, our AI does not guess or hallucinate. Every triage decision is strictly bounded by WHO and Indian Medical Association Standard Treatment Guidelines. Rule C-104 identifies acute cardiac risk, bypasses general OPD queues, and books an emergency teleconsultation with Senior Cardiologist Dr. Smita Rao."</div></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>🩺 ACT IV: Doctor Teleconsultation Desk & Real-Time CDSS (02:50 - 03:40)</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 15%;">Timestamp</th>
    <th style="width: 40%;">Screen Action (/doctor/consultation/...)</th>
    <th style="width: 45%;">Voiceover & Audio Direction</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>02:50 - 03:15</strong></td>
    <td><strong>[WEBRTC VIDEO + CDSS]</strong> 1. Dr. Smita Rao joins teleconsultation room.<br/>2. Patient vitals from ASHA intake load automatically on side-panel.<br/>3. Amber <strong>CDSS Banner</strong> warns: <em>"Hypertensive Urgency (BP 148/92, SpO2 94%)"</em>.</td>
    <td><div class="quote">"Dr. Smita Rao joins the teleconsultation via secure WebRTC video. The doctor doesn't just see a face; JanCare's Clinical Decision Support System provides the entire longitudinal history—flagging the hypertensive urgency recorded hours earlier by the ASHA worker."</div></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>03:15 - 03:40</strong></td>
    <td><strong>[DIGITAL RX]</strong> 1. Doctor prescribes: <em>Tab. Telmisartan 40mg + Tab. Atorvastatin 20mg</em>.<br/>2. Recommends: <em>Coronary Angiography</em>.<br/>3. Clicks <strong>"Sign & Issue ABHA-Compliant Digital Rx"</strong>.</td>
    <td><div class="quote">"Dr. Rao prescribes evidence-based generic medications and electronically signs an ABHA-compliant digital prescription that immediately reflects in Ramesh's patient vault."</div></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>💳 ACT V: The Cashless Revolution — PM-JAY ₹5L Wallet Pre-Auth (03:40 - 04:15)</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 15%;">Timestamp</th>
    <th style="width: 40%;">Screen Action (Doctor Pre-Auth -> Patient Wallet)</th>
    <th style="width: 45%;">Voiceover & Audio Direction</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>03:40 - 03:58</strong></td>
    <td><strong>[SURGERY PRE-AUTH]</strong> 1. On Doctor Desk, open <strong>"PM-JAY Surgery Pre-Auth"</strong> drawer.<br/>2. Select: <strong>Coronary Angiography (CR-402, ₹42,000)</strong>.<br/>3. Click <strong>"Submit Pre-Authorization"</strong>.<br/>4. Green approval modal appears.</td>
    <td><div class="quote">"Recognizing the cardiac risk, Dr. Rao initiates instant Ayushman Bharat PM-JAY pre-authorization for a coronary angiography directly from her desk. Within seconds, the pre-auth request is verified against national package CR-402."</div></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>03:58 - 04:15</strong></td>
    <td><strong>[ZOOM ON PM-JAY WALLET]</strong> Cut to Patient Dashboard (`/patient/dashboard`):<br/>• Total: <strong>₹5,00,000</strong> -> Balance: <strong>₹4,58,000</strong> (Live ₹42,000 deduction).<br/>• Passbook shows transparent transaction hash.</td>
    <td><div class="quote">"On Ramesh’s dashboard, his ₹5,00,000 cashless wallet balance updates in real-time. The patient walks into the district empanelled hospital with pre-approved cashless coverage—eliminating predatory middlemen and financial panic."</div></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>💊 ACT VI: Closed-Loop Jan Aushadhi Dispensation & District Radar (04:15 - 04:40)</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 15%;">Timestamp</th>
    <th style="width: 40%;">Screen Action</th>
    <th style="width: 45%;">Voiceover & Audio Direction</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>04:15 - 04:28</strong></td>
    <td><strong>[GENERIC DRUG RESERVATION]</strong> 1. On Patient Rx tab, click <strong>"Reserve at Jan Aushadhi (90% Savings)"</strong>.<br/>2. Generates token <strong>JC-MED-8492</strong>.<br/>3. Switch to Pharmacist Desk (`/pharmacist/dashboard`) -> enter token -> click <strong>"Dispense"</strong> (Stock auto-decrements).</td>
    <td><div class="quote">"For post-consultation medications, Ramesh reserves generic drugs at the nearest Jan Aushadhi Kendra with one click. Pharmacist verifies token JC-MED-8492, dispenses the generic medicines, and reduces the patient's out-of-pocket drug cost by 90%."</div></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>04:28 - 04:40</strong></td>
    <td><strong>[EPIDEMIOLOGICAL RADAR]</strong> Switch to District Admin (`/admin/dashboard`):<br/>Show Maharashtra Outbreak Heatmap. Click <strong>"Trigger Automated ICMR Containment Alert"</strong> (dispatches SMS to 42 ASHA workers).</td>
    <td><div class="quote">"Simultaneously, every vital recorded across hamlets feeds into our District Epidemiological Radar, enabling health authorities to detect emerging viral clusters 14 days early and automatically trigger containment protocols."</div></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>🏆 EPILOGUE: National Impact, Scalability & Pitch (04:40 - 05:00)</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 15%;">Timestamp</th>
    <th style="width: 40%;">Screen Action</th>
    <th style="width: 45%;">Voiceover & Audio Direction</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>04:40 - 04:52</strong></td>
    <td><strong>[4-QUADRANT IMPACT SLIDE]</strong><br/>
    • 100% ABDM & NHA Standard Compliant<br/>
    • ₹18,500 Avg. Annual Family Savings<br/>
    • Zero-Drop Offline PWA Architecture<br/>
    • WHO / IMHA Certified Clinical Guardrails</td>
    <td><em>(SFX: Orchestral Grand Climax)</em><br/>
    <div class="quote">"JanCare is not a conceptual mockup. It is an end-to-end, ABDM-compliant, production-grade digital public good that protects rural citizens from misdiagnosis, medical debt, and infrastructure failure."</div></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>04:52 - 05:00</strong></td>
    <td><strong>[CLOSING TITLE CARD]</strong><br/>
    JanCare Logo • Team Credits • GitHub: <strong>github.com/SumitKSinghDev/JanCare</strong></td>
    <td><div class="quote">"JanCare: Delivering specialist healthcare and financial dignity to the last citizen of Bharat. Thank you."</div></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<div class="box">
  <h3>📋 Pre-Recording Directorial Checklist:</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Reset Wallet:</strong> Go to Patient Dashboard -> PM-JAY Tab -> Click "Reset to ₹5,00,000" before recording.</li>
    <li><strong>Pre-Load Tabs:</strong> Keep 5 browser windows ready (ASHA, Patient, Doctor, Pharmacist, Admin).</li>
    <li><strong>Video & Audio Standards:</strong> 1080p, 60 FPS, Browser zoom at exactly 100%, Mouse cursor halo enabled.</li>
    <li><strong>Background Music Level:</strong> Keep background tech music at -24 dB during narration; swell at 04:40 mark.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

